{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10","id":1539557,"title":"Blood Potency 10","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-30T13:26:09-07:00","id":1539557,"title":"Blood Potency 10","content":"What would an elder of that high blood potency be capable of? I know that thousand years of night gives good examples of stats and disciplines, but what are they actually capable of? And for a second question if any have ever shown up in your games what did they do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T06:34:23-07:00","id":1539585,"title":"","content":"I would stat such a being with +18 dots of Disciplines, ~9 Devotions, 18 attribute dots, 36 dots of skills and a shitton of merits. <br /> So the answer is : A lot. That's a creature who's chosen area of expertise he has pretty much mastered, with attributes crossing over into 6/7 range. This is a force to be reckoned with even without disciplines, thow in some disciplines, and the ability to get +20 dice from Vitae/turn. If this elder is combat specced - they'll be wrecking almost anything in a single turn - something like an activation of vigor, will put them in the range of 30-40 Dice for their attack, with so many merits, that probably is a fighting style or something brutal otherwise. <br /> <br /> Although, they probably don't need to try that hard - a single actuation of Dominate or Nightmare will shred through your defenses - they are rolling potentially ~20 dice for that activation. <br /> <br /> Vampire has a lot of auto _&quot;I Win buttons&quot; _, and whichever of these this elder has chosen to learn and invest in, he throws ~over 20 dice to do. MEaning that failure is almost impossible against anyone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T09:06:36-07:00","id":1539591,"title":"","content":"It depends. BP 10 doesn't necessarily implies a HUGE personal power. By raw, you gain 1 BP every 50 years, which means that, living a &quot;normal&quot; life, you can reach that power after 450 years. It's a lot of time and surely a lot of higher stats, but not even a Methuselah. More over, BP can be raised by spending XP (AKA being active in your requiem, or by diablerie) this might speed up the BP raise further.<br /> <br /> So, BP10 it's for sure scaring whatever number of attributes/skills and discipline you have as raw power, but it's not everything.<br /> <br /> That being said, I very rarely introduce in my game kindred above BP 7, but as legend, sleeping boogieman, etc. Those almost almighty creature should appear very rarely to not make them ordinary (this is not a superhero game and them would pretty much match a superhero level of power.<br /> <br /> If you ask what they are capable of, this again depend on how ancient they are. 450 years old BP10 vampire is scaring but it's nothing compared to a 1000-2000 years old one that would probably have all discipline at 5 plus very unique and powerful Devotions. Devotions are what make the real difference after a certain point. So I'd say, BP10 Methuselah (or also lower BP Methuselah) are pretty much capable of anything comes into your mind. Just try to keep the mood aligned with an horror game (I hate the potence 5 earthquake from Masquerade V5 in fact).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-31-2024, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T11:19:38-07:00","id":1539596,"title":"","content":"Yeah, basically the question is which Devotions they have.<br /> <br /> Any splat at 10 in their Power Stat is <b>potentially </b>god-like. If they reached it organically, you can expect them to be virtually unstoppable monsters that can level a city if push comes to shove, and they are probably influential and legendary the world around.<br /> <br /> But that's just potential. A character that reached this level through Diablerie and spending XP solely on BP isn't really that powerful. They can burn through Vitae for some impressive feats, but after a few rounds they're done.<br /> <br /> Vampires receive two benefits from such a high BP: a lot of Vitae and speed to spend it, and access to Devotions that either benefit from this speed or have high BP as a requirement.<br /> <br /> The first benefit is easy to picture: imagine a vampire able to activate every Discipline they have plus healing any and all damage every round. The second is harder, but a Devotion that requires 20 Vitae to activate, or have BP 10 as prerequisite, should be truly monumental.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T11:35:52-07:00","id":1539597,"title":"","content":"Agree. Devotions are truly outside the reach of any possible educated guess. A Devotion, not even that powerful, in the corebook allows to soak a nuke bomb explosion in the face (at least for the very first turn - Juggernaut Gait). A BP 10 kindred with devotions of the same tier, is a god-like being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T13:14:14-07:00","id":1539600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539596#post1539596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, basically the question is which Devotions they have.<br /> <br /> Any splat at 10 in their Power Stat is <b>potentially </b>god-like. If they reached it organically, you can expect them to be virtually unstoppable monsters that can level a city if push comes to shove, and they are probably influential and legendary the world around.<br /> <br /> But that's just potential. A character that reached this level through Diablerie and spending XP solely on BP isn't really that powerful. They can burn through Vitae for some impressive feats, but after a few rounds they're done.<br /> <br /> Vampires receive two benefits from such a high BP: a lot of Vitae and speed to spend it, and access to Devotions that either benefit from this speed or have high BP as a requirement.<br /> <br /> The first benefit is easy to picture: imagine a vampire able to activate every Discipline they have plus healing any and all damage every round. The second is harder, but a Devotion that requires 20 Vitae to activate, or have BP 10 as prerequisite, should be truly monumental.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539597#post1539597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree. Devotions are truly outside the reach of any possible educated guess. A Devotion, not even that powerful, in the corebook allows to soak a nuke bomb explosion in the face (at least for the very first turn - Juggernaut Gait). A BP 10 kindred with devotions of the same tier, is a god-like being.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now I am thinking about a conceptually different case. What about the young vampire that is playing with lots of tricks? Full of devotions even if not too high on any singular discipline nor Blood Potence? Carthians have a merit for learning devotions cheaper, and to get 9-again while activating them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T13:24:54-07:00","id":1539601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539600#post1539600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now I am thinking about a conceptually different case. What about the young vampire that is playing with lots of tricks? Full of devotions even if not too high on any singular discipline nor Blood Potence? Carthians have a merit for learning devotions cheaper, and to get 9-again while activating them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite get the point here. To have devotions you need the disciplines they require. If so, you can have as much devotions you want. But also, Devotions are not common knowledge as disciplines are. Should be justified in game why she knows so many Devotions as a young vampire. That being said, I'd said, go for it. It's not game breaking and would make that PC unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 07-31-2024, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T15:28:32-07:00","id":1539665,"title":"","content":"As far as sheer power goes, such a Neonate wouldn't be all that potent, mainly because they can't use their whole arsenal at once.<br /> <br /> But that would be a hell of a versatile vampire, which means they're probably equipped to deal with most of their problems and live longer than most of their rivals. At least as long as they keep a low profile.<br /> <br /> In general it's good to have a mixed approach. Diversifying your power set is more immediately useful, but after a while it has diminishing returns. At the end of the day, you'll need to be able to punch hard in someway if you want to be a serious player (so to speak), and that means high level on your main disciplines at the very least, but also increase BP when you're comfortable with your basic power set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T16:35:21-07:00","id":1539669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539601#post1539601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But also, Devotions are not common knowledge as disciplines are.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has never sat comfortably with me. <i>Some</i> devotions are incredibly weird, but, say, Quicken Sight? I can see a vampire just falling into that one. And the various Resilience-based &quot;you can't do what I do to me&quot; devotions updated and collected under Stalwart Mind in Chris Falco's Devotion to Power seem pretty obvious too. To say nothing of the powers that were redefined as devotions in the switch from 1e to 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":".  I still say Fortitude when I'm not thinking about it 08-01-2024, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T18:52:41-07:00","id":1539671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539669#post1539669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That has never sat comfortably with me. <i>Some</i> devotions are incredibly weird, but, say, Quicken Sight? I can see a vampire just falling into that one. And the various Resilience-based &quot;you can't do what I do to me&quot; devotions updated and collected under Stalwart Mind in Chris Falco's Devotion to Power seem pretty obvious too. To say nothing of the powers that were redefined as devotions in the switch from 1e to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between being able to conceive of the conceptual blending of two abilities and being able to do the legwork needed to consistently develop a <i>new magical power</i> that does not come naturally to you as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Any schmuck with one eye and a working brain can be put onto the basic idea of having a car that is also a boat, but it is substantially more of a process to create such a boat, particularly given the survivorship bias of vampires is such that anyone who puts the time into making it work knows that being one of the few vampires who can teach that trick is a bargaining chip worth guarding jealously to pry blood and other assets from their peers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T04:11:15-07:00","id":1539687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539671#post1539671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between being able to conceive of the conceptual blending of two abilities and being able to do the legwork needed to consistently develop a <i>new magical power</i> that does not come naturally to you as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Any schmuck with one eye and a working brain can be put onto the basic idea of having a car that is also a boat, but it is substantially more of a process to create such a boat, particularly given the survivorship bias of vampires is such that anyone who puts the time into making it work knows that being one of the few vampires who can teach that trick is a bargaining chip worth guarding jealously to pry blood and other assets from their peers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see that, just not always. As an example, I can see that experimentation or tutoring would be required to achieve Enchantment <i>or</i> Behind the Throne (Devotion to Power), but once you had one the other should be simply a matter of Experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T06:20:05-07:00","id":1539688,"title":"","content":"I think this is not the concept which has driven the devotion design. Obviously there're devotions more common and known. You know the effect, you don't even need a teacher e.g.: quicken sight.<br /> But to me, devotions are developed by personal experimentation, bringing diversification among kindred.<br /> You might expect that the mekeht you're talking with now is scanning your thought, much less that he's able to align his mind to yours during a fight, adding his Auspex to his defense (custom devotion between Auspex and Celerity).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T07:47:25-07:00","id":1539692,"title":"","content":"In my games increasing BP allows the vampire to learn one devotion spontaneously, as their blood mutates and further personalizes to them. Others need bigger effort, or teachers. <br /> <br /> However, overall, there's not that much text which says that devotions are as _rare_ as some of the posters above are trying to make them out to be. And IMO, they shouldn't be. They're cool fun toys to play with, and they're also cool things to have as _common_, their variety makes each individual vampire more unique, and provides potential surprises whenever you face an unknown vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T08:14:40-07:00","id":1539695,"title":"","content":"No one is saying the text states that. <br /> It's not they're rare because these are harder to achieve, they're not by design as they only requieres half of the disciplines' total as px cost. Simply while disciplines are mostly known by any kindred having contacts with other kindred for some time, Devotions are, by design peculiar manifestation of difderent disciplines working in sinergy, that basically makes me think it's less common to be aware about a devotion developed by a kindred on his own to be able to replicate and spread its knowledge out.<br /> Devotions are designed to ve flexible and custom powers and the ones proposed by the booka are only samples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-02T09:42:29-07:00","id":1539705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539692#post1539692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, overall, there's not that much text which says that devotions are as _rare_ as some of the posters above are trying to make them out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;These powers are not developed naturally and the people who develop them don't share them for free&quot; is not a statement of rarity, it is a statement of scarcity. Devotions require effort to develop and vampires only have so much time in the night to spend on R&amp;D without building the habits and resources that let them get Vitae to stay active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T18:16:24-07:00","id":1539774,"title":"","content":"I've always assumed that after a few decades most kindred have a Devotion or two, but the vast majority are weird niche devotions they developed on their own rather than coming from any kind of standard list. The same general powers will pop up again and again, but they're not always being done in the same way.<br /> <br /> Plus single Discipline Devotions are a thing, which is as good a justification as many for vampires to not see Disciplines as the preset paths that we know as players, but more general categories of powers that occasionally develop in weird ways. Sometimes a vampire just learns to do something different, and they're highly unlikely to tell you how they did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T21:39:37-07:00","id":1539779,"title":"","content":"It honestly does not seem like Blood Potency 10 is that common among elders, even though the natural rate of Blood Potency progression would seem to indicate that most vampires would attain it after a relatively short time. 1e mentioned elders going into torpor to thin their blood more than 2e does, but it still seems like it is supposed to a be a relatively common thing for elders to do. Perhaps the acquisition of political power and status would allow one to actually have a better chance at maintaining such a high Blood Potency. If an elder gets a ton of Kindred vassals, then they could theoretically maintain a high Blood Potency indefinitely while avoiding any Blood Bonds. Otherwise, the elder would probably need some strong Disciplines in order to be able to hunt other Kindred effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T23:41:35-07:00","id":1539782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539779#post1539779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It honestly does not seem like Blood Potency 10 is that common among elders, even though the natural rate of Blood Potency progression would seem to indicate that most vampires would attain it after a relatively short time. 1e mentioned elders going into torpor to thin their blood more than 2e does, but it still seems like it is supposed to a be a relatively common thing for elders to do. Perhaps the acquisition of political power and status would allow one to actually have a better chance at maintaining such a high Blood Potency. If an elder gets a ton of Kindred vassals, then they could theoretically maintain a high Blood Potency indefinitely while avoiding any Blood Bonds. Otherwise, the elder would probably need some strong Disciplines in order to be able to hunt other Kindred effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I do agree that BP 10 Is rare and difficult to reach/mantain because of feeding restrictions, &quot;hunting&quot; other kindred is not the only means they have.<br /> They have cults, merits, rituals etc that allow them to be fed by other kindred willinglly, without incurring in vinculum.<br /> If not wrong, but can't be 100% sure now, even just Unmarked Grave (protean 1), mentions that the blood spilled on the soil can be used as nurishment without provoking blood bond, while it's never specified that doesn't count as kindred blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 08-04-2024, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T02:34:49-07:00","id":1539784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539774#post1539774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus single Discipline Devotions are a thing, which is as good a justification as many for vampires to not see Disciplines as the preset paths that we know as players, but more general categories of powers that occasionally develop in weird ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. That's an idea that's been bouncing around in my brain for a while, but that I have struggled to express.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 08-04-2024, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T12:35:21-07:00","id":1539797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539591#post1539591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends. BP 10 doesn't necessarily implies a HUGE personal power. By raw, you gain 1 BP every 50 years, which means that, living a &quot;normal&quot; life, you can reach that power after 450 years. It's a lot of time and surely a lot of higher stats, but not even a Methuselah.</div> </div> </div> </div>That <i>does</i> entail the obstacle of having spent over a century of being only able to consume vampire blood, with no innate resistance to the way consuming vampire blood gradually enslaves you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539596#post1539596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any splat at 10 in their Power Stat is <b>potentially </b>god-like. If they reached it organically, you can expect them to be virtually unstoppable monsters that can level a city if push comes to shove, and they are probably influential and legendary the world around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I always have a lot of difficulty being satisfied with the idea of great supernatural power being expressed as large scale destructive capability. I think it's got limited narrative applicability, I don't like the extent to which it can detract from their requirements to leverage command over others, and it often just plain strikes me as unimaginative. I often want to try and envision greater power in terms of depth rather than scale; something that functions on a more personal level, but has a <i>very</i> profound effect.<br /> <br /> Besides, when it comes to Chronicles vampires, I think it's more in keeping that the mightiest of them would kill massive numbers of people more in the vein of Imperfect Cell than Frieza. One at a time, but... quickly. And with unsettling stealth.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-04T12:41:59-07:00","id":1539798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539779#post1539779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It honestly does not seem like Blood Potency 10 is that common among elders, even though the natural rate of Blood Potency progression would seem to indicate that most vampires would attain it after a relatively short time. 1e mentioned elders going into torpor to thin their blood more than 2e does, but it still seems like it is supposed to a be a relatively common thing for elders to do. Perhaps the acquisition of political power and status would allow one to actually have a better chance at maintaining such a high Blood Potency. If an elder gets a ton of Kindred vassals, then they could theoretically maintain a high Blood Potency indefinitely while avoiding any Blood Bonds. Otherwise, the elder would probably need some strong Disciplines in order to be able to hunt other Kindred effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone here thinks it is common. It isn't.<br /> <br /> While it is possible to get there in 450 years without XP, the downside is actually too much of a hassle to keep for two centuries straight. It's not so much about how many ways you have to make it work, but how many things can go wrong during this time.<br /> <br /> A vampire that reaches BP 10 has a dogged dedication to get there and stay. Overall any BP above 5 should be seen as temporary, even for Methuselah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-05T05:27:47-07:00","id":1539847,"title":"","content":"Remember that 6+ attributes and skills don't disappear with Blood Potency anymore, and Vitae/turn gets diminishing returns as you have less and less to spend it on.<br /> <br /> The big benefit to high blood potency in the long run? I think it's actually supernatural resilience. It's not big, it's not flashy, but if you pursue that road your response to a mind whammy is just 'no'. Or when over splats get involved an inherent immunity to being set on fire or turned into a lawn chair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T04:25:48-07:00","id":1540125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539797#post1539797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, when it comes to Chronicles vampires, I think it's more in keeping that the mightiest of them would kill massive numbers of people more in the vein of Imperfect Cell than Frieza. One at a time, but... quickly. And with unsettling stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the Rampage devotion in Better Feared, if you haven't. It does what you're talking about.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T11:15:28-07:00","id":1540133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1539797#post1539797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Personally, I always have a lot of difficulty being satisfied with the idea of great supernatural power being expressed as large scale destructive capability.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's less that this is the only or best expression, and more that this is the simplest way to describe in the context of a short-ish answer. And I didn't said they would have a single supernatural power capable of leveling cities or influencing the world, in fact I didn't said they would need supernatural powers necessarily.<br /> <br /> Even because few powers in VtR work on scale, even at high levels they're usually more depth. I actually think a balance between the two approaches is more fulfilling, but that's neither here or there. In the end I pictured precisely a vampire with a global spanning web of agents, some under supernatural effects, but most not, plus their mere legend having some weight, and a vampire leveling a city one building or person at a time, not in a single blow, but that's the end result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T12:11:55-07:00","id":1540138,"title":"","content":"I think that having a stronger blood potency should mean that your use of Disciplines are more efficent and less chance of failure in it use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T14:19:31-07:00","id":1540143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1540138#post1540138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that having a stronger blood potency should mean that your use of Disciplines are more efficent and less chance of failure in it use.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you model greater efficiency? Also I gather that when you say &quot;less chance of failure&quot; you mean something other than the existing increased likelihood of winning a Clash of Wills. How would that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T17:10:45-07:00","id":1540154,"title":"","content":"A greater chance of winning a clash of wills would definitely be a part of it and perhaps a reroll bonus with a strong blood potency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-10T18:20:19-07:00","id":1540160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1539557-blood-potency-10?p=1540154#post1540154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A greater chance of winning a clash of wills would definitely be a part of it and perhaps a reroll bonus with a strong blood potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were talking about what the game already has. But that aside, high BP gives you access to higher stats, which already make for more reliable rolls.<br /> <br /> Most Disciplines that require rolls already add to the roll, and BP gives you more Vitae to activate Disciplines. All in all, I think it has already a good impact on such powers, plus the advantage on a Clash of Wills.<br /> <br /> But if you think BP lacks supernatural advantages, which I think is a fair concern, I would add it elsewhere, as a power specific to it instead of more dice on Disciplines. In general it should focus on improving what every vampire does, and maybe in overall survivability.<br /> <br /> I don't know, from the top of my head, maybe damage that would destroy a vampire could first reduce their BP instead? I don't know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}